WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.500
Taiwan's top chip maker posted a 55% sales jump last month as demand for AI chips keeps rising. This is Omni View, episode 199. Taiwan's

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:25.840
semiconductor manufacturing company recorded September net revenue of $511.86 billion new Taiwan dollars. That figure marks a 54.6% increase from the same month a year earlier. The

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.180
The company stands as the world's largest contract chipmaker, and supplies advanced

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.160
chips to clients that include Invidia and Apple.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.480
Third quarter revenue reached approximately $1.49 trillion new Taiwan dollars.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.640
Taiwan's semiconductor manufacturing company also announced it will adopt ASML's high

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.820
NA extreme ultraviolet lithography machines.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:53.640
Those machines enable production of even smaller and more powerful chips.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:00.640
CNBC frames the results as evidence that demand for AI hardware remains strong even as foundation

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.200
models improve and pricing pressure grows.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.480
The same report notes that sales did not set a new monthly record.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.040
That correction adjusted an earlier description of the figures.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.600
The company has become a central supplier in the global semiconductor chain because it produces

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.980
the most advanced chips used in artificial intelligence systems.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:25.860
Taiwan's government supported this industry through consistent policy, education investment,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.880
and infrastructure long before artificial intelligence became prominent.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.740
Other countries have tried to build similar capacity but face higher costs, longer timelines,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.060
and gaps in the supplier ecosystem.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.880
What happens next?

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.720
The first compliance deadlines for related equipment adoption fall in coming months.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.940
Yemen's internationally recognized government launched a new military operation this week,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.720
targeting Houthi held areas on the Red Sea coast, in Merib and Al-Jauf.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.280
The government is urging tribes and Houthi-controlled regions to join the fight.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.840
It points to recent limited advances as signs the balance may be shifting.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.640
Many tribes have remained neutral in the past because of the Houthi's military strength

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.480
and earlier failed uprisings.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:16.500
Al Jazeera reports that the offensive follows Houthi gains in September that included capture

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.940
of the port city of Mokha and territory near the Bob Al-Mandeb Strait.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:26.680
The outlet notes that airstrikes have inflicted losses on Houthi forces, but that pushing

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.680
into strongholds such as Sanaa remains difficult.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:35.660
Tribal leaders in Merib held a rally announcing mobilization to support the armed forces and

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:36.860
restore state control.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:42.080
The report emphasizes that tribes will watch whether government gains become sustained

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.200
before deciding whether to shift allegiance.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.580
The United Kingdom retained its existing travel warnings for several Kenyan counties

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:55.120
and added information about Kenya's response to its first imported case of Bundibugio

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.840
virus disease.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.340
That disease is a form of Ebola.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.760
The foreign, Commonwealth, and development office advises against all travel to Mandera

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:10.040
County, parts of Wajir County, Garissa County, outside specific towns, and La Mou County

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.180
except two islands.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.400
Kenyan health authorities have activated contact tracing and monitoring for the imported

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:16.760
case.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:22.200
All Africa reports that the advisory attributes the main restrictions to terrorism risks

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.500
from groups based in Somalia, rather than the health situation.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.000
The update clarifies that the Ebola case is imported and that the Kenyan government

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.840
has put response measures in place.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:37.700
The British government warns that ignoring the advice could invalidate travel insurance.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.020
The restrictions on northern and coastal areas remain unchanged from previous security

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:43.760
based guidance.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:49.200
Israel said most British diplomats and the consul general will leave the consulate in

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.540
occupied East Jerusalem.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.700
That move leaves a task force of seven with limited activity.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:00.020
The United Kingdom stated that some staff were temporarily withdrawn for security reasons,

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:05.880
but that the building will remain open and operate as a UK mission working with the Palestinian people.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.060
The move follows UK sanctions on Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.880
BBC coverage presents the Israeli decision as retaliation for the sanctions,

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.820
which Britain views as responses to settlements that are illegal under international law.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:27.380
Al Jazeera reports UK Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband stressing that the mission will continue its work.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.740
Israeli Foreign Minister Gideon Tsar wrote that the reduction came after Britain imposed

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.780
the sanctions. Both outlets note that the building itself will not close.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:43.460
Chinese AI agent developer Manus secured more than $500 million in a funding round led

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:50.440
by Boyu Capital and IDG Capital. Participation came from Tencent, HSG, and Gen Fund.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:56.400
The round follows Beijing's order forcing meta to unwind its roughly $2 billion acquisition

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.260
of the company.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.920
Investors appear undeterred by the regulatory intervention.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.840
CNBC reports that Bloomberg had previously indicated the financing would double-manus's

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.300
valuation to $4 billion.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.140
That valuation would make it China's most valuable AI agent-maker.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.360
The outlet quotes Eurasia Group analyst Dan Wang saying the short-term fallout from

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.940
the Medicaid has been contained.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:26.440
And Asia Group Analyst Han Lin notes the immediate task for Manus is proving scale, profitability,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.080
and regulatory alignment.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.320
Mauritius Commercial Bank recorded an increase in net interest income for the full year.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:39.020
Chief Executive Terry Hebrod linked that increase to geopolitical tensions driving up oil

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:39.980
and gas prices.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.280
The bank operates across several African markets.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.120
Bloomberg coverage presents the results as evidence that current energy market conditions

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.520
are supporting banking performance in the region.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.820
Hebron discussed the earnings alongside the formation

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.300
of a new Africa Credit Ratings Agency.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.100
The interview frames higher commodity prices

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.100
as a factor boosting interest income

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:04.180
for institutions with exposure to energy-related activity.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.140
South Africa's Department of Home Affairs

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.680
condemned claims that it initiated the suspension

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.060
of good cause interviews for asylum seekers.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:16.100
The Constitutional Court had ruled in July 2026

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.060
that certain provisions of the Refugees Act were unconstitutional.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:26.040
Those provisions included rules allowing deportation of asylum seekers lacking a transit visa.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:34.400
The department stated the ruling was binding and that disinformation campaigns falsely attributed the change to ministerial or political initiative.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:42.140
All Africa reports the department statement that the case was vigorously opposed by the department before the court issued its decision.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:47.380
The ruling affects how asylum applications are processed and removes the requirement

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.940
for good cause interviews in some circumstances.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.920
The department emphasized that the judgment followed a challenge brought by the Scalabrini

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.220
Center of Cape Town, represented by lawyers for human rights.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:04.080
The clarification aims to correct public understanding of the court's role versus government action.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:10.480
To really understand how advanced chip production became concentrated in one company, consider

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:16.000
Consider the decades of accumulated expertise, enormous capital, and stable access to specialized

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:20.000
equipment required to build and operate the necessary fabrication plants.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:26.200
A useful check is to ask which specific equipment or process steps remain difficult to duplicate

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:31.120
elsewhere, and how quickly new facilities outside Taiwan are actually coming online.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:37.940
CNBC frames the revenue release as proof of sustained AI hardware demand, while regional

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:43.040
coverage in Asia places greater emphasis on the structural risks of supply chain concentration.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:48.660
Watch whether tribal leaders in Merib sustain their announced mobilization in the weeks ahead,

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:54.080
as government forces press the offensive. That wraps up today's OmniView. Remember,

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:59.740
the best informed people read more than one perspective, and the calmest ones know that most days

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:05.660
somewhere, something is quietly getting better. For full source links, check out today's written

